## What import reads

These become objects in Paperclip:

- `.paperclip.yaml` — the agents map with each agent's adapter, per-agent monthly budget, the board-approval gate, the projects map, and routine schedules
- `agents/<slug>/` — one agent each
- `projects/<slug>/PROJECT.md` — one project each
- `tasks/<slug>/TASK.md` — one task each
- `skills/<slug>/SKILL.md` — one skill each

These are documentation for you, and have no counterpart object:

{% if has_operations %}
- `OPERATIONS.md` — the operating manual
- `PROJECT-INVENTORY.md` — the deliverable inventory
{% endif %}
- `COMPANY.md` — read in part: the company name and description are imported, the identity body (north star, we are / we are not, constraints, goals) is not

